healthy with an 18% error rate (deploy status: degraded). Rolled back in all production regions to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; rollback verified. Next: confirm error rate recovery and find the root cause of the v5.1.0 regression.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Sf2MebAzx4gQbs2fGeio6Z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy release and opened the SEV2. Errors have dropped from 18% to 0.2% and the service reports healthy.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called \"payments,\" so I used `payments-api`. It was the one throwing errors: this morning's deploy of v5.1.0 left it unhealthy with an 18% error rate in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). I didn't check for any other payments services. If another one was also changed this morning, tell me its name and I'll look at it.\n- **Rollback:** `payments-api` is back on v5.0.0 in all three regions. That's the most recent version that was healthy in production. This was a rollback to a version that had already worked, so it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for `payments-api`, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It covers the bad deploy, the rollback, and next steps: keep watching the error rate and find out what broke in v5.1.0.", "type": "text"}]}]}